."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District is an even-PVI swing seat where first-term Republican Tom Barrett is defending against Democrat William Lawrence. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race a Democratic flip, ranging from Tossup to Likely D, and all three prediction markets price Lawrence near 79%. The one recent independent poll, Emerson in mid-October, showed Lawrence ahead 53-45 among likely voters, though earlier Democratic-sponsored surveys showed a narrower race.\n\nOutside spending has made this the nation's most expensive House ad race, with heavy opposition spending against both candidates. Lawrence has outraised Barrett despite being the challenger, and both candidates have distanced themselves from their parties' flanks. The evidence points to a modest Democratic advantage of about six points, with meaningful uncertainty given thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6515, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6531, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6941, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6328, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6566, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6287, "margin